<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Humanitarian partnership principles">
  <div><strong>Safe water first</strong><span>No hydration product can compensate for unsafe preparation water or weak sanitation.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Use the right formulation</strong><span>Therapeutic diarrhoeal dehydration requires appropriately formulated ORS.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Build locally</strong><span>Partners, logistics, training and community context determine whether a project works.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Implementation before branding</p>
    <h2>Shipping product is not the same as solving the problem</h2>
    <p>Safe water, storage, preparation, local supply, health guidance and continuity all matter. Where therapeutic oral rehydration is required, World Health Organization / UNICEF standards and local clinical guidance should control the intervention.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Ways to collaborate</p>
  <h2>Start small and define the job</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Pilot access project</h3><p>Test a defined use case at small scale with local oversight.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Research partnership</h3><p>Study preparation, adherence, logistics or other implementation questions.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Distribution partnership</h3><p>Explore supply where product fit, regulation and infrastructure make sense.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Program design</h3><p>Integrate hydration into a broader health or community program.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">What we will not blur</p>
    <h2>Consumer hydration and therapeutic ORS are different</h2>
    <p>The current Best Hydrate formula and World Health Organization reduced-osmolarity ORS should not be treated as interchangeable because they share glucose and electrolytes.</p>
    <p>The intended use, formulation and regulatory pathway must match the problem being addressed.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Project fit</span>
    <h3>Bring the local context first.</h3>
    <p>Tell us the location, population, water and health infrastructure, local partners and the problem you are trying to solve.</p>
    <a class="bhd-page__button" href="/pages/contact">Discuss a Project</a>
  </aside>
</section>

